# Firebase client config — TRACKED on purpose.
#
# google-services.json, GoogleService-Info.plist and lib/firebase_options.dart
# all carry the SAME values. firebase_options.dart was always tracked, so
# ignoring the other two hid nothing and only broke fresh clones (the Google
# Services Gradle plugin fails without google-services.json).
#
# A Firebase apiKey is not a credential. Google: "API keys restricted to
# Firebase services do not need to be treated as secrets, and it's safe to
# include them in your code or configuration files." It is also recoverable
# from any release APK. What protects the project is App Check, API key
# restrictions and server-side authorization.
#
# The real secret is the Firebase SERVICE ACCOUNT key — it lives in
# ispoon-backend/.env and is ignored below.

# Environment & keys
*.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
